re warning him and now when dan  asks Tony for help no one responds  because Dan never grows older when they  all do remember the true not starves to  death  Rose comforts and by reminding him of  his super long life out living  civilizations she mentions skyscrapers  which could be a nod to a really dark  subplot in the dr. sleep book in which  Abra as a toddler predicts the 9/11  attacks and the true not visits Ground  Zero to feed off the steam of the  victims avarice family house number is  1980 the year The Shining was released  and the wall that Dan nabber used to  talk breaks into the word murder  reflecting as Redrum in Dan's mirror now  this is the opposite of the way the  mirror was used in the shining  Danny wrote Redrum on the door the  mirror reflected his true meaning murder  so it's reversed here to remind Danny of  the truth in the mirror reflection that  truth being Redrum the nonsense word he  wrote on the door in the Overlook  showing him the place he must eventually  return dan and Abra head to the Overlook  to trap rose Mike Flanagan actually  reused the exact footage of Kubrick's  opening aerial shots of Glacier National  Park rendering them now to look like  it's nighttime with falling snow this  film also throughout resamples shining  music editor Gordon stain for its  chilling sound design with the Eklund  chants and high-pitched shrieks Dan's  stroll through the hotel is shot in  these same camera movements that Kubrick  used  Steadicam tracking shots slow dollies  he's framed it just as his father was  through the crack in the door  and then he literally follows in his  father's footsteps to the Gold Room  where just like his father  he looks directly into the camera and  finds Lloyd the bartender except it's  not Lloyd from before it's a man who's  always been the caretaker here Jack  Torrance now jack is not played by Jack  Nicholson here he's played by Henry  Thomas collaborator if Flanagan from the  hunting of Hill House and a so grown